##CASE lessence-mxv template_present=<KEY_VALUE>
##WHY the key-value detector fires by default; paired with the case below,
##WHY this proves --disable-patterns does something rather than nothing
##FROM the flag was a silent no-op for several detector names
level=info msg="a" component=core

##CASE lessence-mxv template_present=level=info
##WHY --disable-patterns key-value really disables it
##FROM lessence-9h5 was the same bug in LogWithModuleDetector
##FLAGS --disable-patterns key-value
level=info msg="a" component=core

##CASE lessence-arch-2026-08-r98.13 template_present=<EMAIL>
##WHY --sanitize-pii masks an email address
##FROM masking used to apply in some output modes and not others
##FLAGS --sanitize-pii
user alice@example.com logged in from the console

##CASE lessence-w3k template_present=<SECRET>
##WHY --sanitize-pii masks a credential-class assignment and terminates
##FROM the masking loop used to be able to spin forever
##FLAGS --sanitize-pii
service token=sk-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx accepted

##CASE lessence-arch-2026-08-r98.8 out_absent=\e[
##WHY --preflight strips terminal escapes before analysing
##FROM preflight was the one mode that skipped escape stripping
##FLAGS --preflight
INFO \e[31mdisk failure\e[0m on node

##CASE lessence-m2p out_absent=\e[
##WHY the full terminal escape set is stripped by default, not just CSI
##FROM a crafted log line could smuggle escapes into a terminal
INFO \e[31mdisk failure\e[0m on node

##CASE lessence-ino out_present=```
##WHY --format markdown fences log content so it cannot be interpreted as markup
##FROM untrusted log content used to be emitted into the document body
##FLAGS --format markdown
ERROR **bold** and [link](http://x) and | pipe

##CASE lessence-arch-2026-08-r98.10 err_present=--format markdown supports only the default fold output
##WHY an unsupported --format combination is refused out loud, not silently
##WHY  downgraded to text
##FROM the format flag used to be dropped by --top, --summary and --fit
##FLAGS --format markdown --top 1
a 1
a 2
a 3
b 1

##CASE lessence-lst out_absent=(showing top
##WHY --format json --top N keeps stdout pure JSONL; the human header goes to stderr
##FROM the header used to be printed to stdout and broke every JSON parser
##FLAGS --format json --top 1
a 1
a 2
a 3
b 1

##CASE lessence-748 out_absent=Compression Report
##WHY the statistics footer never lands on stdout under -q
##FROM stats used to pollute the piped output
a 1
a 2
a 3

##CASE lessence-7ga out_present=INFO
##WHY --summary truncates a long non-ASCII line without cutting mid-character
##FROM the truncation used to slice on a byte offset and panic
##FLAGS --summary
INFO anvandaren kunde inte autentiseras mot servern med ett mycket langt meddelande som maste trunkeras nagonstans i mitten av ett tecken aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa

##CASE lessence-arch-2026-08-r98.10 exit=2
##WHY refusing an unsupported --format combination also fails the process, so a
##WHY  pipeline notices
##FROM paired with the err_present case above; kills a mutant that prints and exits 0
##FLAGS --format markdown --top 1
a 1
a 2
a 3

##CASE lessence-fiz out_present=# Log Analysis
##WHY --format md renders markdown rather than silently emitting text
##FROM the alias used to be accepted and then ignored
##FLAGS --format md
a 1

##CASE lessence-fiz out_present="type":"group"
##WHY --format JSON is case-insensitive and renders JSON, not text
##FROM the alias used to be accepted and then ignored
##FLAGS --format JSON
a 1

##CASE lessence-9h5 template_present=<BRACKET_CONTEXT>
##WHY the bracket/log-module detectors fire by default; paired with the case
##WHY  below, this proves --disable-patterns reaches them too
##FROM LogWithModuleDetector consulted no config at all
[Wed Oct 11 14:32:52 2000] [error] [client 127.0.0.1] mod_jk child workerEnv in error state 6

##CASE lessence-9h5 template_present=[error]
##WHY --disable-patterns brackets really leaves the bracketed level alone
##FROM the flag was accepted and then ignored by this detector
##FLAGS --disable-patterns brackets
[Wed Oct 11 14:32:52 2000] [error] [client 127.0.0.1] mod_jk child workerEnv in error state 6

##CASE lessence-arch-2026-08-r98.9 out_present="lines_saved":1
##WHY lines_saved, output_lines and compression_ratio agree with each other and
##WHY  with the fold: 4 lines in, one group, one line saved, 25 percent
##FROM the three used to be computed separately and disagree across modes
##FLAGS --format json
req took 111 ms
req took 222 ms
req took 333 ms
req took 444 ms

##CASE lessence-arch-2026-08-r98.9 out_present="compression_ratio":25.0
##WHY the ratio is derived from the same fold as lines_saved, not recomputed
##FROM paired with the case above; kills a mutant that fixes one and not the other
##FLAGS --format json
req took 111 ms
req took 222 ms
req took 333 ms
req took 444 ms
